{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/831585-crossovers","id":831585,"title":"Crossovers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-17T01:21:17-08:00","id":831585,"title":"Crossovers?","content":"I ran a campaign a number of years ago in which I used the critters from the various WoD lines (both oWod and CofD) as antagonists in addition to and in replacement of the ones in the books. It was definitely a learning experience. Whilst the rules were close enough to make use possible, it was not a smooth transaction and definitely showed some of the flaws in Scion that I hope will be addressed in 2e. That being said, it was a blast and a half, giving the PC's something to do other than Titan-hunting. They quickly learned not to assume that a problem they encountered was Titan related, which helped encourage a sense of mystery that made the game much more interesting. <br /> <br /> Anybody else given this a try and, if so, what was your experience like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Yes, yes, yes... I know it is a horror game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11143-feonorx","name":"Feonorx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T23:39:36-08:00","id":833074,"title":"","content":"I used the Classic World of Darkness as my setting for my three Year Scion Game, it was very Excellent at Hero Level but like with the rest of the Scion System it got wonky at Demigod level.<br /> <br /> It was fun riding a Train through the Dreaming, the Morgan Scion having one of the Morgan Corax as a Mentor, Vampires in particular were oodles of fun, and they got mixed up with the Technocrats trying to stop the end of the World and one of the Mortal Parents of a Scion was a Euthanatos with a Serial Killer Wraith as a Follower. In another game the Samedi Scion had a Samedi vampire as a Mentor and Risen as Followers. The best part is virtually none of the players knew either setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T07:34:46-08:00","id":833248,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/7193425/1/The-Scion-of-Athena\" target=\"_blank\">This story</a> is the beginning of a series in which a Scion of Athena is accidentally scattered across multiple realities. Some of them belonging to the World of Darkness line, others belonging to alternate White Wolf games (such as Exalted) and some not even related at all (such as X Men).<br /> <br /> Of course when you take a Demigod level Scion and throw it into these other realities, it equates to a Mary Sue insertion. Such as when she manages to singlehandedly slay a 2nd circle level demon from Exalted. Or when she made their craftsmen seem like primitive savages... or when she blasted an entire Sabbat raid into dust...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T13:11:14-08:00","id":837732,"title":"","content":"I could see Mage: the Ascension crossed with Scion. The themes mesh fairly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T20:00:14-08:00","id":837886,"title":"","content":"I actually use some of the fluff from nWoD and the creatures. A lot of Vampire and Werewolf fluff is canonically in my game. I just use Scion's system to build them up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T23:02:56-08:00","id":843303,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of doing that with exalted 3e, with Hero level = heroic God blooded ESS 1-3, Demigod = 4-5 Ess god/second circle demon , and Gods= lesser Incarna/head of Bureaus/3rd circle demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11217-kurseteller","name":"kurseteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}